.TH WM2TJ 1 "2026-10-22" "wm2tj 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wm2tj \- minimal X11 window manager with vertical tabs, based on wm2
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm2tj
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wm2tj
is a window manager for the X Window System based on wm2 by Chris Cannam.
Every window gets a tab on its left edge, drawn bottom to top, with the
window title and a close button, and a thin frame.  It takes no options and
is normally started by
.B wm2-session
from the "wm2tj" entry of the display manager's session list, which also
starts the compositor, the top bar and the other helpers that are installed.
.PP
Compared with wm2, wm2tj draws titles with Xft and UTF-8, has maximise and
minimise, virtual desktops, EWMH support (so taskbars, pagers and docks work
and maximised windows stay clear of them), a root menu with cascading folders
and a search box, and a configuration file.
.SH MOUSE
.TP
.B Left button on a tab
Raise and focus the window; drag to move it.
.TP
.B Double-click on a tab
Maximise the window, or restore it.
.TP
.B Middle button on a tab
Minimise (hide) the window.  Minimised windows are listed in the root menu
and in the top bar.
.TP
.B Left button on the bottom-right corner of the frame
Drag to resize the window.
.TP
.B Left button on the close button
Close the window.
.TP
.B Right button on the root window
Open the root menu: favourites, application folders, the open windows, and
the session commands (restart, log out, shut down).  Typing in the search
box at the top filters every application and open window.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from
.I ~/.wm2rc
at start-up and again on
.BR SIGHUP .
One setting per line,
.I keyword value
; a
.B #
starts a comment.  Colours are X colour names or
.BR \(dq#RRGGBB\(dq .
The main keywords:
.TP
.BI font " xft-pattern"
Font of the tab labels, e.g. "Noto Sans CJK JP:style=Bold:pixelsize=13".
.TP
.BI menufont " xft-pattern"
Font of the root menu.
.TP
.BI tab_width " px"
Thickness of the tab (default 32; 0 fits the font).
.TP
.BI tab_length " px"
Length of the tab (default 220; 0 fits the title).
.TP
.BI tab_gloss " colour" | none
Base colour of the glossy gradient on the tab, or
.B none
for a flat tab in
.BR tab_background .
.TP
.BI tab_foreground " colour"
Colour of the tab label.
.TP
.BI button_background " colour"
Colour of the close button.
.TP
.BI borders " colour" | none
Colour of the frame lines, or
.B none
for no lines.
.TP
.BI frame_background " colour"
Colour of the frame.
.TP
.BI menu_background " colour" ", " menu_foreground " colour"
Colours of the root menu.
.TP
.BI desktops " n"
Number of virtual desktops.
.TP
.BI new_window " command" ", " new_label " text"
Command run by the "new window" entry of the root menu, and its label.
.TP
.BI double_click_time " ms"
Longest interval between two clicks on a tab that still counts as a
double-click (maximise).
.TP
.BI click_to_focus " yes" | no
Focus follows clicks rather than the pointer.
.PP
.B wm2tj-settings
edits the appearance settings in a window and applies them at once;
.B wm2tj-favorites
edits the favourites of the root menu.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Re-read
.I ~/.wm2rc
and the menu, keeping every window and the current desktop:
.B pkill \-HUP \-x wm2tj
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.wm2rc
Configuration.  Created at the first login of the session from
.I /usr/share/wm2tj/wm2rc.sample
(the settings) by
.BR wm2-menu-gen ,
which appends the root menu below a marker line and leaves what is above it alone.
.TP
.I ~/.config/wm2tj/favorites
Favourites of the root menu, shared with
.BR wm2tj-bar (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wm2tj-bar (1),
.BR wm2-swipe (1),
.BR picom (1)
.PP
https://github.com/wm2tj/wm2tj
.SH AUTHORS
wm2tj is based on wm2, written by Chris Cannam and others.  wm2tj is an
independent fork by tetsu and is not affiliated with or endorsed by the
original author.
